From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZagWrt <zagwrt@localhost>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] an7581: add uboot chainloader for gemtek xg2010g

Same rationale as the Gemtek W1700K chainloader (see
999-airoha-add-gemtek-w1700k.patch): the Econet XG2010G ships with a
bootloader-locked vendor U-Boot that manages its own BMT/BBT on the
W25N04K SPI-NAND (512 MiB). Directly flashing/booting a modern
upstream FIT kernel image via the vendor `bootm` resets the board.

This adds a standalone U-Boot (no BL2/BL31 rebuild needed, those are
shared an7581 blobs) that can be packaged as a FIT "kernel" and
chainloaded from the vendor bootloader via TFTP + bootm, without
touching flash. Partition layout mirrors the layout already used by
the OpenWrt kernel DTS (target/linux/airoha/dts/an7581-xg2010g-ubi.dts)
so the same UBI volumes (ubootenv/ubootenv2/fit/factory) are visible
to both U-Boot and Linux. LED/button GPIO numbers are taken from the
vendor DTS (phy_tx_power_disable, sts_*, pon_*, lan_led_*, BTN_0),
translated to the unified en7581_pinctrl numbering already verified
in the kernel DTS.

Signed-off-by: ZagWrt <zagwrt@localhost>
